00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:30.070
Hank: There are a lot of different ways to
not make any sense at all, but of all of them,

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:34.129
the fact that some people don't have access
to simple healthcare despite the fact that

00:00:34.129 --> 00:00:39.320
we live at the peak moment of wealth in human
history makes the least sense of all.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:43.050
Partners in Health is dedicated to ending
that weird, lopsided world.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:46.980
They empower and equip local health workers
and have been working with the people on the

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.980
front lines of the fight against ebola before
any of us in the US even knew that there was

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.000
an outbreak.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.559
Ebola is a world health problem.

00:00:53.559 --> 00:00:55.690
Antibiotic resistance is a world health problem.

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:57.920
Pneumonia is a world health problem.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:02.190
No community is exempt from these challenges,
and Partners in Health is doing genuinely

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:07.070
heroic work around the world to save lives,
not just now, but a hundred years from now.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:11.210
Partners in Health is a huge part of the ongoing
success story of increased access to healthcare

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:15.410
and decreased suffering throughout the world,
and through our support, we will also be a

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:16.640
part of that success story.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.680
For the first half of the Project for Awesome,
we'll be splitting the money raised between

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.390
Partners in Health and an equally amazing
organization, Save the Children.

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:28.420
We'll also have matching funds for the first
500,000 dollars donated, meaning that if we

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:33.260
reach 500,00 dollars by noon on Saturday,
a total of a million dollars will be given

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:35.000
to partners in health and Save the Children.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.560
During the second half, the money raised will
be distributed via your votes.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.400
To watch videos promoting charities and vote
on the ones that capture your interest and

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.950
